"""
A plain unittest -- no QEMU, no qemu_test import. There is no passing
transcript yet: the two-chassis boot has never discovered its second hub
on this machine, which is exactly why the leg is red. What can be pinned
is that neither real failure reads as a pass.

Fixture provenance (real captured guest-console text, byte-exact):

  REAL_ONE_NODE_DECLINE
      The console of a project-harness run that netbooted
      MDK_router_sso on ONE node and ran router_sso (2026-08-27): the
      kernel declines with "EXITING router_sso test because there is only
      1 node board in system" and still prints its completion line. A
      pass here would be the classic vacuous acceptance; the marker
      catches it.

  REAL_TWO_CHASSIS_WEDGE
      The console of a project-harness run of the four-CPU two-chassis
      shape (2026-08-28): the PROM finds one hub, prints "Headless HUB
      inaccessible", and loops without reaching the menu.
"""

